<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="lc-ol-introduction">
  <title>Introduction</title>
  <section xml:id="lc-ol-learning-outcomes">
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <p>Learning outcomes describe the knowledge, understanding, skills and values students should be able to demonstrate.</p>
    <p>The Ordinary Level learning outcomes are presented in five course Parts, in syllabus order. Each Part starts with the complete learning outcomes.</p>
    <p>Across the five strands, students should be able to explore patterns, explain findings, justify conclusions, communicate mathematics clearly and apply suitable methods in familiar and unfamiliar situations.</p>
    <p><em>Source:</em> <url href="https://www.curriculumonline.ie/getmedia/f6f2e822-2b0c-461e-bcd4-dfcde6decc0c/SCSEC25_Maths_syllabus_examination-2015_English.pdf" visual="Leaving Certificate Mathematics Syllabus (for examination from 2015)"/>. The published syllabus remains the authority for mathematical notation and scope.</p>
  </section>

