  <section xml:id="lc-ol-opening-and-saving-pdfs">
    <title>Opening and Saving PDFs in Chrome</title>
    <p>If the scheme opens in Chrome, you can read it in the PDF viewer. To keep a copy on your device, select the Download button in the viewer.</p>
    <p>To change the default for the Chrome profile you are using, paste <c>chrome://settings/content/pdfDocuments</c> into the address bar. Select <em>Open PDFs in Chrome</em> to read them in the browser or <em>Download PDFs</em> to save them automatically. This setting applies to PDF links across websites.</p>
    <p>To see or change the save location, go to Chrome Settings and select <em>Downloads</em>. You can also turn on <em>Ask where to save each file before downloading</em>.</p>
  </section>
</chapter>
